{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011ChQVKGv856N7MgMZqs3oL","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"That settles who sets up the plan and how it's split. One part of Q1 is still open, and Q2–5 haven't been answered yet.\n\n**Now settled:** the customer chooses 2, 3, or 4 equal installments. Uneven cents go on the last installment.\n\n**Rest of Q1:** when are the installments due? I recommend one month apart, with the last one on the invoice's current due date. The other option is starting on the current due date and going a month apart after that, so the final payment lands up to 3 months later.\n\n**Still open (my recommendations unchanged):**\n- **Q2. Missed installment:** I recommend (a), only that installment becomes overdue. The alternative, (b), makes the whole remaining balance due at once.\n- **Q3. Reminders:** I recommend (a), one 3 days before each installment. The alternative, (b), is a single reminder before the final due date.\n- **Q4. How payments are applied:** I recommend (a), to the oldest unpaid installment first, with any extra carried forward. The alternative, (b), applies it to the installment the customer picks.\n- **Q5. When customers can choose a plan:** I recommend (a), only while the invoice is `sent` and not yet overdue, and the plan can't be changed afterwards. The alternatives are (b) also allowing it on overdue invoices, or (c) letting customers change the plan later.\n\nIf you reply \"agree\", I'll take all of these recommendations. After that, the only question left is how the late fee works."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2076,"cache_read_input_tokens":33504,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2076},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":nu